# Subject
Outdoor landscape photographs: lakes, forests, and city skylines, across different times of day.

# Emphasise
- Time of day and the quality of light: golden hour, blue hour, overcast, harsh midday.
- Weather and ground conditions that are visible, such as snow cover, wet ground, or haze.
- The vantage point and framing: eye level or elevated, an open vista or an enclosed view.
- Foreground, middle ground and background as distinct layers, named in that order.

# Avoid
- Naming places, landmarks, or people; describe what is visible instead.
- Guessing the season or time of year when the image does not show it.
- Camera, lens, or image-quality commentary.
